## Comparisons

- [Compare](https://tray.ai/compare): Honest comparisons against named competitors.
- [Tray.ai vs. Salesforce Agentforce — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/agentforce): Agentforce is an AI layer built on a CRM. Tray.ai is a purpose-built automation platform for agents and AI across your whole business.
- [Tray.ai vs. Boomi — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/boomi): How Tray.ai compares to Boomi on speed, AI-readiness, pricing model, and platform coherence.
- [Tray.ai vs. Celigo — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/celigo): Celigo is the go-to for NetSuite integration. Tray.ai is the consolidation play when you also need agents, gateway, and orchestration beyond NetSuite.
- [Tray.ai vs. Salesforce / Informatica — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/informatica): Informatica only does data — you still need MuleSoft and Agentforce for everything else. Here's how Tray.ai compares.
- [Tray.ai vs. Jitterbit — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/jitterbit): How Tray.ai compares to Jitterbit on platform coherence, AI-readiness, and the cost of a bundle built through acquisition.
- [Tray.ai vs. Make — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/make): How Tray.ai compares to Make (formerly Integromat) on governance, scale, AI readiness, and enterprise suitability.
- [Tray.ai vs. Microsoft Power Automate & Logic Apps — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/microsoft): How Tray.ai compares to Microsoft's integration stack — one orchestration layer vs. a patchwork of Azure services.
- [Tray.ai vs. MuleSoft — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/mulesoft): How Tray.ai compares to MuleSoft on scope beyond Salesforce, implementation time, TCO, and platform consolidation.
- [Tray.ai vs. n8n: an honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/n8n): n8n is a good way to build. What changes at production is who owns the risk. Tray.ai takes the patching, the scaling and the audit evidence, so the platform gets easier to run as it grows, not harder.
- [Tray.ai vs. Oracle Integration Cloud — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/oracle-oic): OIC is great for Oracle-to-Oracle integration. Tray.ai is what Oracle-running enterprises use when they also need non-Oracle, non-integration, and AI.
- [Tray.ai vs. SAP Integration Suite — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/sap): SAP Integration Suite is built for connecting SAP systems. Tray.ai is built for everything — SAP included, not SAP-centered.
- [Tray.ai vs. SnapLogic — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/snaplogic): SnapLogic is a 20-year-old data pipeline tool retrofitting AI agents. Tray.ai is a unified platform built for integration and agents from day one.
- [Tray.ai vs. TIBCO — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/tibco): How Tray.ai compares to TIBCO (now Cloud Software Group) on AI readiness, modern cloud architecture, and time-to-value for enterprise integration and orchestration.
- [Tray.ai vs. Workato — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/workato): How Tray.ai compares to Workato on builder flexibility, AI-readiness, pricing, and enterprise fit.
- [Tray.ai vs. Zapier — honest comparison](https://tray.ai/compare/zapier): How Tray.ai compares to Zapier on enterprise scale, complex workflows, governance, and AI-native capabilities.

